        <item>
            <title>2.19.0</title>
            <pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 15:56:59 +0900</pubDate>
            <link>https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy</link>
            <sparkle:version>95</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.19.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>15.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Features

- **Drive the MacroPad from another Mac.** The pad and the Canopy it controls no longer have to be the same machine: run `scripts/macropad-bridge.sh` on the Mac holding the pad, choose **Remote bridge** on the other, and the keys and LEDs work over Tailscale. One transport at a time — the machine serving its pad must have MacroPad set to Off.
- **The sidebar's MacroPad indicator is now the source selector.** It used to only report the link state; clicking it opens Off / Local / Remote. The thing that shows the state is the thing that changes it, so switching no longer means a trip to Settings or the menu bar.

### Changes

- **The unread LED lights for the pane you left focused.** It never did before: the keystroke that sends a prompt satisfied every clearing condition at once — it attributed the session, reset presence, and proved Canopy was frontmost — so sending a prompt cleared the completion of the very turn it started. A mark now clears only on an act that comes *after* the turn finished.
- **Clicking a lit pane, or its sidebar row, acknowledges it.** Clicks only counted when they moved focus, which meant the pane most likely to be lit — the one you left focused when you walked away — was the only one a click could not acknowledge.
- **The indicator no longer disappears when the MacroPad is off.** It draws a slashed glyph instead, because a control that vanishes in the state it reports cannot be used to leave it — and the machine most in need of the switch is exactly the one that has to be off to serve its pad over the bridge.
- **Sparkle updated to 2.9.6.** Both releases since the previous pin are security fixes on paths Canopy uses: 2.9.5 hardens delta patching against a symbolic link at the destination, and Canopy ships delta updates; 2.9.6 hardens the installer's handling of the download archive, rejects package installs whose signature failed validation, and fixes a privilege escalation.

**Full changelog**: https://github.com/Saqoosha/Canopy/compare/v2.18.0...v2.19.0
]]></description>
